---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { products } from '../../data/products';

const slugOrder = [
  'cyberpower-cp1500pfclcd',
  'apc-br1500ms2',
  'apc-bx1500m',
  'apc-be600m1',
];

const picks = slugOrder.map(slug => products.find(p => p.slug === slug)!);
const topPick = picks[0];

const bestFor: Record<string, string> = {
  'cyberpower-cp1500pfclcd': 'Best Overall — Modern PCs',
  'apc-br1500ms2': 'Best Premium — Brand Name Pure Sine',
  'apc-bx1500m': 'Best Mid-Range — Standard Desktops',
  'apc-be600m1': 'Best Budget — Routers & Basic Setups',
};

const waveform: Record<string, string> = {
  'cyberpower-cp1500pfclcd': 'Pure Sine Wave ✓',
  'apc-br1500ms2': 'Pure Sine Wave ✓',
  'apc-bx1500m': 'Simulated Sine Wave',
  'apc-be600m1': 'Simulated Sine Wave',
};
---

<Layout
  title="Best UPS Battery Backup for Home Office (2025) — APC vs CyberPower, Pure Sine vs Simulated"
  description="The best UPS battery backup units for home offices — covers pure sine wave vs simulated, how much VA you need, runtime estimates, and honest picks from APC and CyberPower."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">

    <!-- FTC Disclosure -->
    <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-md p-3 mb-6 text-sm text-yellow-800">
      <strong>Disclosure:</strong> HouseGearGuide earns a commission if you buy through our links — at no cost to you. We only recommend products we've researched thoroughly.
    </div>

    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
      <a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a> &rsaquo;
      <a href="/backup-power/" class="hover:underline">Backup Power</a> &rsaquo;
      <span class="text-gray-700">Best UPS Battery Backup for Home Office</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Best UPS Battery Backup for Home Office (2025)</h1>

    <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
      A UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply) is not a generator — it won't run your office for hours. It gives you 10–30 minutes of clean power when the grid drops: enough to save your work, finish a video call, or gracefully shut down. For a home office where an unexpected outage means lost work, a missed meeting, or a corrupted file, a UPS is one of the most practical purchases you can make.
    </p>

    <!-- Critical Buying Info Box -->
    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg p-4 mb-8 text-sm text-red-900">
      <strong>Read this before buying:</strong> If your desktop PC was built after 2010, it almost certainly has an <strong>active PFC (aPFC) power supply</strong>. These require a <strong>pure sine wave UPS</strong> — a simulated sine wave UPS can damage them or cause them to shut down immediately during a power event. Check your PSU specs or just buy pure sine to be safe.
    </div>

    <!-- Top Pick Box -->
    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-lg p-5 mb-8">
      <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">Top Pick — Best Home Office UPS</div>
      <div class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">{topPick.name}</div>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">{topPick.tagline}</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-700">${topPick.price}</span>
        <a href={topPick.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="bg-orange-500 hover:bg-orange-600 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-md text-sm transition-colors">
          View on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Comparison Table -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Quick Comparison</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-gray-200">
        <thead class="bg-gray-100">
          <tr>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">UPS</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Best For</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Capacity</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Waveform</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Outlets</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Price</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Link</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {picks.map((p, i) => (
            <tr class={i % 2 === 0 ? 'bg-white' : 'bg-gray-50'}>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 font-medium">{p.name}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-xs text-green-700 font-medium">{bestFor[p.slug]}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2">{p.specs['Capacity']}</td>
              <td class={`border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-xs ${waveform[p.slug].includes('✓') ? 'text-green-700 font-semibold' : 'text-gray-600'}`}>{waveform[p.slug]}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2">{p.specs['Outlets']}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2">${p.price}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2">
                <a href={p.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">Amazon →</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- Individual Product Reviews -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Full Reviews</h2>

    {picks.map((p, i) => (
      <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
          <div>
            <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">
              #{i + 1} — {bestFor[p.slug]}
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">{p.name}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1">{p.tagline}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-right flex-shrink-0">
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-700">${p.price}</div>
            <div class={`text-xs mt-0.5 font-medium ${waveform[p.slug].includes('✓') ? 'text-green-600' : 'text-gray-500'}`}>
              {waveform[p.slug]}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm mb-4">
          {Object.entries(p.specs).map(([key, val]) => (
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded px-3 py-1.5">
              <span class="font-medium text-gray-700">{key}:</span> {val}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
          <div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-green-700 mb-1 text-sm">Pros</div>
            <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
              {p.pros.map(pro => <li class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="text-green-500 mt-0.5">✓</span><span>{pro}</span></li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-red-600 mb-1 text-sm">Cons</div>
            <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
              {p.cons.map(con => <li class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="text-red-400 mt-0.5">✗</span><span>{con}</span></li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a href={p.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="inline-block bg-orange-500 hover:bg-orange-600 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-md text-sm transition-colors">
          Check Price on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>
    ))}

    <!-- Buying Guide -->
    <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">UPS Buying Guide for Home Office</h2>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">How Much VA Do You Need?</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2">VA (volt-amps) is the UPS capacity rating. As a rough rule, your UPS should be rated for at least 1.25× the total wattage of connected equipment.</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <table class="w-full text-xs border-collapse border border-gray-200">
          <thead class="bg-gray-100">
            <tr>
              <th class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 text-left">Setup</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 text-left">Approx. Draw</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 text-left">Recommended UPS</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="bg-white"><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Router + modem + streaming box</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">50–100W</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-medium">APC BE600M1 (600VA)</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Laptop + monitor + router + NAS</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">150–250W</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-medium">APC BX1500M (1500VA)</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-white"><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Desktop PC + monitor + router</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">300–500W</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-medium">CyberPower CP1500PFCLCD — pure sine required</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Gaming PC + 2 monitors + peripherals</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">500–800W</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-medium">APC BR1500MS2 — pure sine required</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Pure Sine vs. Simulated Sine — The Real Difference</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
        Grid power is a smooth sine wave. A pure sine UPS replicates that exactly — every device runs as if plugged into the wall. A simulated (stepped) sine wave is a rough approximation: fine for older power supplies, desk lamps, and basic electronics, but can cause modern aPFC power supplies to malfunction, shut down immediately, or draw excessive current during the transition. If you're protecting a desktop PC bought after 2010, buy pure sine.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Runtime Is Shorter Than You Think</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
        A 1500VA UPS running a 500W desktop gets roughly 8–12 minutes of runtime. That's by design — UPS units are meant to bridge the gap to a graceful shutdown or generator startup, not to run your office for an hour. If you need longer runtime, look at a portable power station or home battery backup instead.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Replace the Battery Every 3–5 Years</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
        UPS batteries degrade silently. A unit that shows "charged" may only provide 2–3 minutes at real load if the battery is 5 years old. Most brands sell replacement batteries for $30–60. The APC BR1500MS2 has user-replaceable batteries that swap in 5 minutes. Budget for this — it's cheaper than replacing the whole unit.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Guides -->
    <div class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Related Guides</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li>→ <a href="/backup-power/best-backup-power-home-office/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best Backup Power for Home Office (Portable Stations)</a></li>
        <li>→ <a href="/backup-power/best-portable-power-station-under-500/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best Portable Power Stations Under $500</a></li>
        <li>→ <a href="/backup-power/best-whole-home-battery-backup-system/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best Whole-Home Battery Backup Systems</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
